  "id": "COMPOUND:22287 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Astersaponin F is implicated in the regulation of CX-1 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is a common target across several compounds, including Astersaponin F, Javanicoside F, and Ascidiathiazone B, suggesting a shared biological role in cellular signaling. The presence of a consistent target relationship between Astersaponin F and CX-1, despite the involvement of different upstream targets, indicates a potential mechanistic link that is not yet fully elucidated. The evidence suggests that Astersaponin F may modulate the activity of this kinase, which in turn affects CX-1, but further investigation is needed to determine the exact nature of the interaction and its functional significance. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the kinase in mediating the effects of Astersaponin F on CX-1, though the precise mechanism remains to be determined.",
